  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 720.12, when the auditor identifies a material misstatement of fact in the other information, the auditor should discuss the matter with management and request correction. Even though the error is unrelated to the financial statements, it may undermine the credibility of the document containing the audited statements.
Wrong (B): The auditor cannot ignore a material misstatement of fact in the other information. AU-C 720 imposes a responsibility to address such errors even when unrelated to the financial statements.
