  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 450.A2, clearly trivial misstatements are those that are inconsequential individually and in the aggregate, of a wholly different magnitude than materiality. A $12 error against $50,000 materiality is well below any reasonable threshold and need not be accumulated.
Wrong (A): Projection to the population applies to misstatements found through sampling, not to individually identified items that are clearly trivial.
Wrong (B): Communication to governance applies to significant matters. A clearly trivial amount does not require such communication.
Wrong (D): A judgmental misstatement arises from differences in management estimates or accounting policy judgments, not from a minor rounding error.$EXPL$
