-- Q5018: Misstatements and Control Deficiencies [easy/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 450.08 and AU-C 265.A5, even when management corrects identified misstatements, the auditor should consider their nature and cause. A pattern of 15 cutoff errors suggests the revenue cutoff control is not operating effectively, which may constitute a significant deficiency or material weakness requiring communication.
Wrong (A): Withdrawal from the engagement is an extreme response reserved for situations where the auditor cannot form an opinion. A pattern of corrected errors does not warrant withdrawal.
Wrong (C): Withdrawing the prior-year opinion is unrelated to current-year control deficiency evaluation. The pattern of errors pertains to the current period''s controls.
Wrong (D): Recalculating materiality using a lower benchmark is not the appropriate response. The concern is about control effectiveness, not about the materiality threshold.$EXPL$
