UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 560.14, when the auditor becomes aware of facts that existed at the report date that may have caused a material misstatement, the auditor must discuss the matter with management and determine whether the financial statements need revision. The $500,000 error exceeding $300,000 materiality requires prompt action.
Wrong (A): Taking no action is inappropriate when the auditor learns of a material misstatement in previously issued financial statements. AU-C 560 imposes a continuing obligation.
Wrong (B): Deferring to the next year''s audit is insufficient for a known material misstatement. The auditor must address the issue promptly rather than waiting.
