UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 265.05-.07, the three severity categories are control deficiency (the base level), significant deficiency (serious enough to merit governance attention), and material weakness (reasonable possibility of undetected material misstatement). These are the specific terms used in the standard.
Wrong (A): Minor, moderate, and critical is not the classification hierarchy established by AU-C 265. These terms are not used in auditing standards for control deficiency severity.
Wrong (B): Inconsequential, reportable, and material are not the categories defined by AU-C 265. "Reportable" was used in older standards but has been replaced.
