-- Q5309: Misstatements and Control Deficiencies [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 265.A14, fraud of any amount is a strong indicator that a significant deficiency or material weakness exists. Even though $35,000 is below $500,000 materiality, the presence of fraud signals that controls failed to prevent or detect unauthorized transactions, elevating the deficiency''s severity.
Wrong (A): The fraud-related nature is highly relevant to severity evaluation regardless of dollar amount. AU-C 265.A14 specifically identifies fraud as an indicator of elevated severity.
Wrong (C): While fraud often results in a material weakness, the auditor must still evaluate severity based on facts and circumstances. Automatic classification is not required.
Wrong (D): Detecting fraud during the audit does not reduce the severity assessment. The control failure that allowed the fraud to occur is the relevant consideration.$EXPL$
